  "tail": 1.8,
  "handle": "@hootexplains",
  "scene": "money",
  "music": "music/bed.wav",
  "hook": {
    "line1": "BANKS CREATE MONEY",
    "line2": "OUT OF THIN AIR",
    "top": "14%"
  },
  "outro": {
    "line1": "DID YOU KNOW",
    "line2": "BANKS DO THIS?",
    "top": "11%"
  },
  "beats": [
    {
      "text": "Jake's bank just created 20,000 dollars out of thin air.",
      "speed": 1.25,
      "shot": "loanHook",
      "event": "hook",
      "highlight": [
        "created",
        "thin"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "You'd think it lent him someone's savings. Nope.",
      "speed": 1.2,
      "shot": "vaultMyth",
      "event": "myth",
      "highlight": [
        "savings",
        "Nope"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "When it approves his car loan, the bank just types 20,000 into his account. Brand new money.",
      "speed": 1.25,
      "shot": "laptop",
      "event": "types",
      "highlight": [
        "types",
        "new"
      ],
      "hold": 0.4
    },
    {
      "text": "Not a conspiracy theory. The Bank of England published it.",
      "speed": 1.25,
      "shot": "laptop",
      "event": "source",
      "highlight": [
        "England"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Episode 2 of 6. Follow along.",
      "speed": 1.25,
      "shot": "car",
      "event": "cta",
      "highlight": [
        "Follow"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "So why can't banks make infinite money? Two catches.",
      "speed": 1.2,
      "shot": "car",
      "event": "rehook",
      "highlight": [
        "infinite"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "One: when Jake pays the loan back, that money disappears.",
      "speed": 1.25,
      "shot": "repay",
      "event": "repay",
      "highlight": [
        "disappears"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Two: they need borrowers who'll repay, and the Fed steers what borrowing costs.",
      "speed": 1.25,
      "shot": "fed",
      "event": "limits",
      "highlight": [
        "repay",
        "Fed"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "But when money grows faster than the stuff to buy, prices tend to rise. Did you know banks did this?",
      "speed": 1.25,
      "shot": "loanHook",
      "event": "final",
      "highlight": [
        "prices",
        "banks"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
